  "instruction_rows": 981,
  "stdout_lines": 1030,
  "complete_fact_body": "Actual reader /root/resource_media_serialized_cloud. Fixed original R Game.exe. All seven callback PE units below were personally read in full: 981 instruction rows, 1030 stdout lines. Every disassembled byte matches the original fixed executable. Exact spans, SHA, complete stdout/stderr and actual UTC/exit are in native-font-followup-005. These functions close only their own source bodies. All business NOT_EXECUTED, UPDATE_NOT_STARTED.\n\nThe common premise is that the previously received candidate truetype descriptor is selected and registered, its objects/stream/service/allocator are valid, and callbacks normally return. Its registration and actual active-font path remain OPEN. This is not proof the embedded font was loaded, executed or displayed.\n\nMED-NFONT-6A6DC0, complete 2938 B / 714 instructions. Face initializer obtains the service named exactly \"sfnt\" through 68bc40; no service returns 0x0b. It seeks the stream to zero through 692cc0, invokes the service +0x08 initial parser, then accepts the reported scaler types 0xa56b6264, 0x74727565, 0xa56c7374, 0x00010000 or 0x00020000. Other types return 2. It sets face flag 0x800. Negative face index returns after the initial parser/type guard. Otherwise service +0x10 performs the next initialization and its error propagates.\n\nThe initializer then checks complete family-name rules and three-table fingerprints to set flag 0x2000. A leading six-uppercase-letter plus-sign subset prefix can be skipped for the name test. Every one of twenty fixed 20-byte patterns is considered by the called string-search helper: cpop, DFGirl-W6-WIN-BF, DFGothic-EB, DFGyoSho-Lt, DFHei, DFHSGothic-W5, DFHSMincho-W3, DFHSMincho-W7, DFKaiSho-SB, DFKaiShu, DFKai-SB, DFMing, DLC, HuaTianKaiTi?, HuaTianSongTi?, Ming(for ISO10646), MingLiU, MingMedium, PMingLiU, MingLi43. The search helper body remains OPEN, so substring behavior is not independently certified from its call shape alone.\n\nWithout a name match, it visits the entire SFNT table directory, marking the presence of cvt, fpgm and prep. It considers all 31 fixed fingerprint rows, each containing checksum/length for those three tables. Matching length is required first; when needed it seeks/reads complete table content and computes a 32-bit sum of four-byte words with trailing bytes shifted into high-order positions. Read failures do not become successful matching checksums. Absent tables can match only their zero-length components. A row counter reaching three sets flag 0x2000. All 31 rows, including their six exact integers, are retained in native-font-driver-contribution.json and were read. This is actual program predicate data, not a hash substitute for reading font programs. In particular none of the 31 cvt lengths is 648; conditional on the actual cvt length and table-directory delivery remaining 648, this fingerprint path has no matching row regardless of table checksum. It does not certify the service's runtime field population.\n\nThe routine requests hdmx through face +0x2a0. A successfully found table longer than seven bytes is read through 692ec0; its big-endian record count must be 1..255, and normalized record size must equal the rounded glyph-count-based stride. It allocates a pointer array, records only records fitting the actual table end, sorts those pointers through 80b218/699f20, and stores table length/count/stride. Invalid/unsupported header shape releases the reached frame and zeroes table count. Allocation/read errors follow their explicit return paths; this is not a universal malformed-font acceptance claim.\n\nWhen the tested face flags or incremental interface require glyph processing, absence of incremental data causes glyf lookup and location handling. Missing-table low byte 0x8e is treated specially by setting glyf length zero; other errors propagate. A loca lookup failure returns 0x90. The loca length is capped according to short/long format to 0x20000/0x40000, derives count by shifting by 1/2, and compares it with glyph count plus one. If too short it examines following table offsets or stream remainder; sufficient room extends the requested frame/count, otherwise glyph count is reduced to the available count minus one. It then reads the frame and propagates the specified read results. This is the complete local range policy; downstream frame/stream helpers remain OPEN.\n\nIt calls 69bd80, accepting zero or low byte 0x8e at the written gate, then separately looks up and reads all fpgm and prep bytes into face +0x3b8/+0x3c8 with their +0x3b0/+0x3c0 lengths. Missing lookup clears that program pointer/length; the frame-read low byte 0x8e is tolerated at those explicit sites, while other errors return. The program bytes are requested/stored here, not interpreted by this function. Later fixed-strike/loca logic counts nonempty glyphs through 699e30; a single nonempty glyph at index zero, or another single glyph whose queried name equals exact \".notdef\", can clear scalable flag 1. Other counts preserve it.\n\nIf the high face-index component and face flag 0x100 require it, 6a1bd0 runs and errors propagate, then 6a6630 is requested. On the final successful path, the initializer installs five concrete local function pointers: face +0x2a8=69ace0, +0x2b0=69ad40, +0x2b8=6997a0, +0x2c0=69b0c0, +0x2c8=69e1e0. The bodies and exact roles of those five callbacks remain OPEN. The caller's face cleanup handles any returned error; this initializer has incremental writes, stream changes and allocations before later failures and does not locally undo all earlier effects.\n\nOPEN transitive source: 68bc40, 692cc0, sfnt service +0x08/+0x10, family string helpers, face +0x2a0 table lookup, 693020/693230/693180/693140 frame/reads, 692ec0/692fe0/692d60, 695140, 80b218/699f20, 69bd80, 699e30, 68b5e0, 6a1bd0/6a6630, installed callbacks, registration and active font selection. Complete program recovery by the dedicated reader is separate.\n\nMED-NFONT-6A5CD0, complete 265 B / 54 instructions. Nil face returns immediately. Otherwise it requests the face +0x3f0 generic finalizer with +0x3e8 data, optional service +0x18 finalization, then releases the reached loca/hdmx/program-related frames and buffers through 692fe0/695370 in the exact stored-offset order. It clears lengths/pointers at +0x434,+0x458,+0x3d8,+0x3d0,+0x3b0,+0x3c0, invokes 6a5a60 and clears +0x410. The helper/callback bodies remain OPEN; freeing requests and field clearing do not prove exception-safe teardown.\n\nMED-NFONT-699DF0, complete 31 B / five instructions. The size initializer writes qword -1 at +0x1a0, byte zero at +0x88, dword -1 at +0x98, and returns 0. It has no children, argument guard, VM interpretation or hidden success result.\n\nMED-NFONT-6A5E80, complete 602 B / 100 instructions. It obtains allocator from the face and, if an execution context at size +0x198 exists, requests 695370 for all five reached context buffers, clearing their pointer/count fields before freeing the context and clearing +0x198. It then requests frees for all reached size-owned arrays/buffers at +0x140,+0x150; for a nonnil secondary allocator at +0x158 it frees/clears +0x188,+0x180,+0x170,+0x168,+0x178 and clears allocator/size fields. Finally it frees +0xa8/+0xb8, clears byte +0x88 and pointers +0xa0/+0xb0/+0xc0, and restores +0x1a0=-1. Every source request and branch was read; 695370's actual freeing behavior and context ownership invariants remain OPEN.\n\nMED-NFONT-69B550, complete 15 B / three instructions. Slot init loads slot +0xf0, then its first pointer, and tail-jumps to 687be0. It adds no local validation or interpretation; 687be0 is OPEN. This wrapper does not itself interpret glyph programs.\n\nMED-NFONT-6A6240, complete 276 B / 80 instructions. Size request first tries service +0xd0 for a face with flag 2. Failure sets selected strike +0x98=-1 and falls back to the already fully received 68a220 metrics calculation. A metrics error returns directly. For a scalable face, the ordinary fallback then calls 699f30, checks its result, chooses resolution based on size metrics (or 72 for scale request/type 4 or zero resolution), and computes size +0x9c through 686130.\n\nSuccessful service strike selection stores the index before further operations. A nonscalable face requests service +0xd8 and resets index to -1 if that call fails. A scalable face calls already received 689ff0, then 699f30; this branch returns the previously zero saved status and does not propagate that last 699f30 result. This is an explicit local status behavior, not proof the callee can fail on this font. Earlier metrics/index writes remain on later errors; no general rollback. OPEN: service callbacks, 699f30 and 686130.\n\nMED-NFONT-69A160, complete 87 B / 25 instructions. Size select stores selected index +0x98 before dispatch. Nonscalable faces use service +0xd8 and reset the index to -1 on error, returning that result. Scalable faces call 689ff0 then 699f30, discard the latter result and return 0. Index validation belongs to the already received outer 68a6a0 and does not appear in this callback. OPEN: service callback and 699f30 behavior.\n\nNo new formal defect is proposed from these static guards or discarded statuses without their concrete reachable premises and separate nonproposer counterreview. The prior two native contributions remain unchanged historical artifacts; this addendum narrows their former callback-body OPEN labels only for these seven exact units. It leaves all transitive missing source and all font-program/host claims explicit.\n",
  "fact_body_file": "native-font-driver-facts.md",
